From d514ceeba0aa8aba39220b2ffdc2a1bd7c3f9f09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:52:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: ROCmFP4 MMVQ becomes opt-in
 (GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ=1) - kept in full, not yet cleared

lane-209 closed rank 7 as MEASURED WIN, INTEGRATION BLOCKED: +26.9% drafted
decode on the ROCmFP4-FAST file, CI [1.3212, 2.7186], 8/8 cells, zero empties -
with the numerical safety of the two retained widths n=3 and n=5 never tested,
because the plain cache-history reproducer that isolated the n=2 first-token EOG
cannot reach n=3. The five rank-7 commits sit linearly between rank 5 and the
lane branch tip, so they cannot be excluded from an integration without
rewriting history. This commit therefore decides the DEFAULT, and changes no
kernel: every line of the mechanism stays exactly where it was.

The gate that decided it was pre-registered before it ran
(lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/r8-integrate/PREREG-r8-integration.md), with
three verdicts rather than two, because a width that never executes is neither
proven safe nor proven unsafe.

ARM A - adversarial op level, CLEAN, with a dispatch receipt.
Six data patterns built to break q8_1 activation quantization (9-decade block
range, f32 denormals, exact sign alternation, all-zero rows, an E2M1 code sweep,
31 octaves of per-block scale), at n=1..5, on the seat row k=5120 and a ragged
9-block k=288, plus the exact 17408x5120 seat shape. 63 cases, 0 materially
worse, 0 NaN, 0 FAIL. The ON-vs-OFF differential is the receipt that the code
under test actually ran: the arms differ at exactly n=3 and n=5 and are
identical at n=1, n=2, n=4 - precisely the r10 gate, so this is not two runs of
the f32 shader agreeing with itself. MMVQ came out CLOSER to the CPU reference
than the f32 shader on every pattern, by 2 to 6 orders of magnitude. That is NOT
read as "more accurate": CHECKED ggml-cpu.c, this type's CPU vec_dot_type is
GGML_TYPE_Q8_0 and its vec_dot is an integer dot, so the reference is itself an
int-quantized-activation path and MMVQ is arithmetically its family member. The
honest reading is the negative one - no adversarial input made the MMVQ path
diverge in a way the f32 path did not.

ARM B - served, ROUTE RECEIPT PRESENT at n=3, NOT byte-identical, no degradation.
Three arms on one binary, one load at a time, on the seated DFlash2 line
(--spec-draft-n-max 2, so the verify ubatch is n_draft+1 = 3): OFF, ON, and a
SECOND ON. The second ON is what makes the first readable - F-141 records that
Vulkan decode is not always reproducible at temp 0 on this box, so without it
"the arms differ" and "the box differs from itself" are the same observation.
Control ON vs ON2: identical 3/3. Test ON vs OFF: 2 of 3 identical; prompt 2
differs by ONE synonym at equal token count (34/34), both arms finishing `stop`,
"improve data transfer efficiency" against "optimize data transfer speed". Zero
empty completions in either arm. The perf logger shows the ON arm executed
ROCmFP4 at n=3. It never executed n=5, and neither did lane-209.

WHY OFF ANYWAY, when both arms came back clean.

Not because the mechanism looks unsafe - it does not. Because it is not CLEARED,
and those are different claims:

  - n=5 is live in the selector and has never run in served generation, here or
    in lane-209. The seated line emits n=3 and never n=5.
  - three prompts is a far weaker probe than the exact-fill cache-history replay
    that found the n=2 defect. That defect appeared on one prompt cell out of
    eight, deterministically, and only under a replayed history.
  - the pre-registered PASS row required byte-identity, and byte-identity did
    not hold. Reading the difference as benign after seeing it - which it plainly
    is - and then calling it a PASS would be moving the goalpost the
    pre-registration exists to hold still.
  - maker != checker. A maker does not certify its own path ON by default.

So the win is preserved whole and costs one environment variable to take:
GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ=1. Nothing is dropped, nothing is reverted, and the
evidence FOR flipping the default is banked beside the evidence that stopped it.
On the seated Huihui line this changes nothing either way - that file carries no
ROCmFP4 tensors at all.

Evidence: research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/r8-integrate/
33-ADV-RESULT.json, 41-SERVE-MMVQ.json, 30-adv-ON.txt, 31-adv-OFF.txt,
40-serve-{OFF,ON,ON2}.server.log, PREREG-r8-integration.md

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Measured-effect: none on the seated line (no ROCmFP4 tensors); on ROCmFP4 files
  this defers a measured +26.9% drafted decode behind an opt-in env var
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
index 95024c63c..017b0aac8 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -10113,6 +10113,38 @@ static bool ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq(const vk_device& device, uint32_t m, uint32_
     // 1.55x (width-3 baseline) - while the f32 dequant shader rises 1.4-1.6x on the same rows, and
     // Q5_K is faster on the f32 shader at every measured n>1 (0.73-0.88x). Route them where they win.
     // GGML_VK_FORCE_MMVQ / GGML_VK_DISABLE_MMVQ (mmvq_mode above) still override this.
+
+    // arifi lane-206: ROCmFP4 MMVQ is OPT-IN. GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ=1 enables the n=3/n=5 route
+    // that the block below describes; without it every width takes the f32 dequant shader.
+    //
+    // The mechanism is a MEASURED WIN and is kept in full - +26.9% drafted decode on the ROCmFP4
+    // file, CI [1.3212, 2.7186], 8/8 cells (lane-209 r10). It ships OFF because it is not yet
+    // CLEARED, which is a different statement from unsafe, and the two must not be collapsed:
+    //
+    //   - n=5 has never executed in served generation. Not in lane-209, and not in the lane-206
+    //     gate either: the seated --spec-draft-n-max 2 line emits n=3 and never n=5, so the width
+    //     is live in this selector and completely unexercised outside test-backend-ops.
+    //   - the lane-206 adversarial op gate came back CLEAN at n=3 and n=5 - six patterns that break
+    //     q8_1 activation quantization, at the seat shape and at a ragged k, MMVQ closer to the CPU
+    //     reference than the f32 shader on every one, zero NaN, zero FAIL - but the CPU reference
+    //     for this type is ITSELF a q8_0 int-dot (ggml-cpu.c, vec_dot_type), so MMVQ agreeing with
+    //     it more closely is partly structural and cannot be read as "more accurate".
+    //   - served ON vs OFF is NOT byte-identical: 1 of 3 prompts diverges by one synonym at equal
+    //     token count with both arms finishing `stop`, against an ON-vs-ON control that reproduces
+    //     3/3. That is the expected consequence of a different numerical path, not a defect - but
+    //     three prompts is a far weaker probe than the cache-history replay that found the n=2
+    //     first-token EOG in the first place.
+    //
+    // So: the evidence is good and the coverage is thin, and this session is the maker. Flipping
+    // the default is an independent checker's call, and costs one line when it is made.
+    if (device->vendor_id == VK_VENDOR_ID_AMD && src0_type == GGML_TYPE_Q4_0_ROCMFP4_FAST) {
+        static const char * rocmfp4_mmvq_env = getenv("GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ");
+        static const bool   rocmfp4_mmvq     = rocmfp4_mmvq_env && rocmfp4_mmvq_env[0] == '1';
+        if (!rocmfp4_mmvq) {
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+
     // arifi lane-209 rank 8: keep ROCmFP4 MMVQ off the n=1 decode path.  This check must remain
     // outside the n > 1 batch-routing block below; placing it inside that block makes n < 2
     // unreachable and silently routes n=1 back through MMVQ.
